  "subject": {
    "id": "maintained-knowledge-history-projection",
    "type": "DOCUMENT"
  },
  "summary": "Implement the operator-activated in-memory reader with atomic verified suffix advancement.",
  "why": "Luis activated the maintained ledger-fed graph after accepting Core ownership. RED 7c29da51 records eleven absent-reader failures; GREEN 851913c0 introduces one public read-only projection using the existing semantic fold. Thirteen reader guards cover supplier action/correction, shipment revision, stale reads, corrupt suffixes, incomplete transactions and atomic publication. Core/history/KG/protocol: 469 passed. Complete Shop: 253 passed. Targeted Recon replay: 7 passed. Ordinary updates decode only appended event bytes and construct only new records; full replay remains recovery. Prefix hashing, copies and canonical receipts remain proportional costs. No database, service, storage format, new knowledge identity, authoritative graph writer, package/version change, release or push. Existing compiler-bound Shop evidence remains byte-identical. Consumer integration stays downstream.",
